      "evidence": "The original endpoint contract annotation asserts both endpoints belong to relative support, but the unchanged Definition requires only at least m+1 support points. On [0,1] the finite positive measure delta_(1/3)+delta_(2/3), m=1, has all required moments and support exactly those two interior points. Thus the annotation is false while the Definition is sound. Replaced only that endpoint assertion with optional endpoint membership and the a<b caveat, preserving its exact source anchor; completed independent Definition/dependency/risk review. No Statement/Definition, manifest or consumer change is needed. See research/numerical-optimization-dynamics-2026-10-16-alpha-batch-82-3a.md.",
